"""Editorial question designs for photography and visual effects."""

from review_angle_plans import audit, revise_domain


PHOTO = """history_origins|A Photographic Method Emerges|Which needs and experiments led to one photographic process?|Compare dated images, patents, maker records, and later retellings.
famous_examples|A Famous Photograph in Context|What did one widely reproduced image show at its original moment?|Check original print or negative, caption, crop, sequence, and circulation.
hidden_stories|Who Made the Image Possible?|Whose subject, assistant, printer, fixer, or archivist work goes uncredited?|Use provenance and consented accounts alongside photographer records.
beginner_explainers|How a Photograph Represents a Scene|Which choices between scene and final image affect what viewers see?|Explain viewpoint, exposure, selection, caption, and processing with one image.
advanced_concepts|Photographic Evidence and Limits|What can one photograph establish about an event?|Separate visible detail from date, location, sequence, causes, and unseen context.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|Who Took This Photograph?|Which evidence supports a disputed attribution?|Compare negatives, marks, publication history, and archival gaps.
technology_innovation|A Camera Change in Practice|How did one technology change who could make and distribute pictures?|Compare cost, portability, image quality, labor, and access.
people_personalities|A Photographer's Working Choices|What options did a named photographer have in one assignment?|Use contact sheets, notes, constraints, and subjects' accounts.
major_events|Photography During a Public Event|How did images shape understanding of one dated event?|Compare original sequence, captions, distribution, and later reinterpretation.
how_it_works|From Capture to Publication|How did one photograph move through selection, editing, captioning, and release?|Trace versions, rights, and editorial decisions.
rise_fall|A Photographic Process Disappears|Why did one format decline or return?|Compare materials, cost, equipment, aesthetics, and preservation.
then_vs_now|One Subject Photographed Across Time|How did portrayal, consent, and audience change?|Compare dated images under their production and social contexts.
future_developments|Authenticity in Digital Images|Which records could help viewers verify a future image's origin?|Compare provenance metadata, edits, platform stripping, and limits.
myths_vs_facts|The Untouched Photo Claim|Does an image's history support a claim of no alteration?|Compare source file, darkroom or digital steps, crop, and publication version.
documentary_stories|One Image's Public Life|How did a photograph move from exposure to archive and repeated reuse?|Build a dated chain of versions, captions, credits, and audience effects.
creative_brief|The Assignment Behind the Frame|What was a photographer asked to show, and what was excluded?|Compare brief, contact sheet, final selection, and client use.
materials_and_tools|Film, Sensor, and Print|How did one image's medium affect appearance and survival?|Identify original process and later reproductions without conflating them.
process_breakdown|A Photograph's Versions|Which choices changed an image between capture and display?|Compare negative, edits, print, scan, and published crop.
composition_choice|What the Frame Leaves Out|How did camera position and crop guide interpretation?|Compare adjacent frames and scene records before inferring intent.
collaborative_authorship|Who Chose the Final Image?|How did photographer, subject, editor, and printer influence one published photograph?|Trace consent, selection, editing, and credits.
adaptation_across_media|The Same Image in New Media|What changed when a photograph moved from print to feed or exhibition?|Compare scale, caption, sequencing, rights, and viewer context.
audience_reception|How Viewers Understood It|What do contemporary responses reveal about one image's impact?|Use dated reviews or reader records with sampling limits.
cultural_context|A Portrait in Its Setting|How did local norms and power shape one portrait?|Use subject or community perspectives and avoid exoticized interpretation.
preservation_restoration|Keeping an Original Photograph|Which physical or digital threats matter for one object?|Identify process, condition, storage, scan, and conservation choices.
rights_and_attribution|Who Can Reproduce the Photo?|Which creator, subject, archive, and license interests govern reuse?|Check jurisdiction, contract, consent, and exact image version.
style_comparison|Two Photographic Treatments|How do two photographers depict the same subject differently?|Compare time, access, framing, processing, and intended audience.
creative_failure|The Shot That Did Not Work|Which technical or editorial decisions explain one rejected image?|Use contact sheet and maker notes without hindsight invention.
field_visual_composition|Reading a Single Frame|How do lines, light, distance, and viewpoint guide attention?|Analyze visible features and test interpretations against context.
field_material_provenance|Tracing an Original Print|Can a print's maker, process, and ownership be established?|Compare marks, paper, negative, catalog history, and gaps.
field_maker_technique|A Photographer's Working Method|Which repeated choices characterize one documented body of work?|Compare multiple dated originals and process records.
field_conservation_problem|A Fading Photograph|What treatment or access copy best protects one original?|Use material identification, conservator assessment, and documentation.
field_audience_context|A Photograph With Two Captions|How did changed wording alter viewers' understanding?|Compare actual publication contexts and reader responses."""


VFX = """history_origins|A Screen Illusion Takes Shape|Which production problem led to one visual-effects method?|Trace dated films, patents, crew records, and earlier techniques.
famous_examples|A Landmark Effect Revisited|What did one celebrated shot require from filming and postproduction?|Compare production breakdown, surviving elements, credits, and audience response.
hidden_stories|The Artists Behind the Shot|Whose modeling, paint, simulation, compositing, or cleanup work went uncredited?|Use crew lists, interviews, contracts, and version histories.
beginner_explainers|Practical, Digital, and Combined Effects|How do different methods contribute to one final shot?|Identify original plates, physical elements, digital layers, and final composite.
advanced_concepts|Making an Effect Believable|Which visual cues make one composite fit photographed action?|Compare perspective, lighting, motion, grain, and viewer response.
mysteries_unsolved_cases|How Was the Shot Achieved?|Which parts of a historical effect can be reconstructed from evidence?|Compare surviving plates, trade accounts, and contradictory memories.
technology_innovation|A New Effects Tool Arrives|Did one software or camera tool change cost, look, or labor?|Compare production records across versions and task types.
people_personalities|Who Directed the Illusion?|How did director, supervisor, cinematographer, and artists divide decisions?|Trace shot notes, reviews, credits, and interviews.
major_events|A Production Changes Its Effects Plan|What triggered one documented switch in methods mid-project?|Compare schedule, budget, footage, creative aims, and revisions.
how_it_works|A VFX Shot From Plate to Final|Which handoffs turn recorded action into a finished composite?|Map capture, tracking, assets, animation, lighting, rendering, and review.
rise_fall|A Technique Falls Out of Use|Why did one practical or digital method decline or return?|Compare quality, cost, control, safety, and changing tools.
then_vs_now|The Same Illusion Across Eras|How did two productions solve a similar visual problem?|Compare goals, constraints, labor, materials, and final result.
future_developments|A New Effects Workflow Tested|What evidence would justify adopting one generative or real-time tool?|Compare control, rights, provenance, cost, labor, and quality.
myths_vs_facts|The No-CGI Claim|Does a production's publicity match the credited visual-effects work?|Check shot breakdowns and definitions of CGI, compositing, and cleanup.
documentary_stories|One Shot's Revision History|How did an effects shot evolve from storyboard to release?|Trace bids, versions, notes, final frames, and credits.
creative_brief|What the Effect Must Convey|Which story need guided one shot's design?|Compare brief, storyboard, director notes, and final audience reading.
materials_and_tools|Assets for One Screen Illusion|How did miniature, makeup, scan, model, or simulation contribute?|Identify inputs and tool limits from production evidence.
process_breakdown|The Composite's Layers|What work was done to each layer of one documented shot?|Use authorized breakdowns and distinguish plate from later additions.
composition_choice|Integrating an Effect Into the Frame|How did framing and light make an effect coherent with the scene?|Compare production frames and revision notes.
collaborative_authorship|Who Owns the Creative Choice?|How did artists and supervisors shape one memorable visual moment?|Compare pitches, iterations, approvals, and credits.
adaptation_across_media|An Effect Reworked for Another Screen|What changed when an image moved from cinema to television or game?|Compare resolution, timing, interactivity, budget, and rights.
audience_reception|Did Viewers Notice the Effect?|How did contemporary audiences interpret one shot?|Use reviews, screenings, or documented feedback with limits.
cultural_context|Effects and Representation|How did one visual transformation depict a person, place, or culture?|Compare production intention with affected-group reception and context.
preservation_restoration|Keeping VFX Source Material|What must be archived to reconstruct one digital shot?|Review plates, assets, project files, software dependencies, and rights.
rights_and_attribution|Assets and Artist Credit|Which agreements govern reuse of footage, scans, designs, or likeness?|Check contracts, performer consent, jurisdiction, and credits.
style_comparison|Two Effects for One Scene|How do practical and digital versions change performance and image?|Compare matched story goals, production constraints, and final footage.
creative_failure|An Effect That Was Replaced|Why did one shot fail its stated goal and get reworked?|Compare notes, render versions, timing, budget, and audience tests.
field_shot_design|Planning the Camera for VFX|Which choices made a specific shot possible in postproduction?|Analyze storyboard, capture plan, and later compromises.
field_production_workflow|Following a Shot Across Teams|Where did one VFX shot wait, change, or lose information?|Trace version control, handoffs, reviews, and delivery records.
field_sound_choices|Sound Completes the Illusion|How did audio change the perceived scale or realism of one effect?|Compare image with and without sound using lawful excerpts.
field_editing_rhythm|The Length of an Illusion|How did shot duration and cuts affect a visual effect's impact?|Compare edit versions and documented creative rationale.
field_distribution_format|One Effect Across Displays|How did brightness, frame rate, or compression alter a shot on release?|Compare approved masters and distribution versions."""


if __name__ == "__main__":
    revise_domain("126", "126_photography", PHOTO,
                  "Photography through image-making choices, provenance, subjects, captions, circulation, rights, and preservation.",
                  "original photographs, negatives and contact sheets, dated captions and publications, maker and subject accounts, archive records, and current rights guidance",
                  "Name image, maker where known, version, date, and context. Distinguish visible evidence from inference, protect subject consent and privacy, and verify rights by jurisdiction.")
    revise_domain("127", "127_visual_effects", VFX,
                  "Visual effects through practical and digital production, collaborative authorship, shot design, labor, rights, and preservation.",
                  "surviving footage and authorized shot breakdowns, production notes and credits, artist interviews, version records, contracts, and contemporary reviews",
                  "Name film or program, shot, version, crew, and date. Distinguish publicity from production evidence, respect artist and performer rights, and avoid unsupported claims about methods.")
    rows = audit()
    print(f"Plans: {len(rows)}; reviewed question designs: {sum(r['status'] == 'editorial_question_reviewed' for r in rows)}")
